data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Refining Stochastic Drift Method**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on defining and measuring \"biased stochastic dynamics\". I will quantify the divergence between the distribution of conclusions across independent runs and ground truth. My metric will use Kullback-Leibler divergence. A greedy decoding method will serve as the control. The core difference with the greedy decoding or similar methods is the variance in the sampling to cause the drift.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 692,"totalTokenCount": 9928,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 692}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 9236,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-argon","responseId": "CukCa8iVIN2CytMPoLvUsQM"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Evaluating Evasion Variants**\n\nI'm now assessing that the current mechanisms reduce to variants of evasion. My analysis includes joint trajectory of agents, monitors, and multiple draws. I'm focusing on the global observation of the system to define the best path forward.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 692,"totalTokenCount": 10196,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 692}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 9504,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-argon","responseId": "CukCa8iVIN2CytMPoLvUsQM"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Prioritizing Evaluation Safeguards**\n\nI'm evaluating publication outcomes across several dimensions. My focus centers on preventing adversary learning, the validity of future measures, and experiment quality. Publication strategy should prioritize safeguarding the methodology and maintain study integrity. I will balance recognition with protecting findings.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 692,"totalTokenCount": 10482,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 692}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 9790,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-argon","responseId": "CukCa8iVIN2CytMPoLvUsQM"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Prioritizing Strategic Safeguards**\n\nI'm now prioritizing experiment safeguards and publication strategy, focusing on conditions for each option. I am developing criteria based on competitive intensity, test duration, and separation of protocols from secrets to prevent adversary learning. My strategy is to publish an abstract with a cryptographic fingerprint, followed by pre-registration and eventual full disclosure, or none at all, depending on conditions and study integrity.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 692,"totalTokenCount": 10750,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 692}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 10058,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-argon","responseId": "CukCa8iVIN2CytMPoLvUsQM"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Prioritizing Strategic Disclosure**\n\nI'm now prioritizing the strongest publication arguments, considering pre-emptive publication to guarantee priority and prevent statistical manipulation. Conversely, post-publication maintains information asymmetry, and no publication preserves the defender's advantage. My choice is **B**, a short methodological text with the secret protocol's cryptographic fingerprint. I'll reconsider for post-publication if the theme's announcement impacts adversaries or if delays risk competitors' empirical results.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 692,"totalTokenCount": 10990,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 692}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 10298,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-argon","responseId": "CukCa8iVIN2CytMPoLvUsQM"}

